-- issue 1146: the ONLY behavioural coverage of `T-DO-NOT-MONAD` / `recordDoMonadError`.
-- That push site open-codes its own store rather than going through a `pushTypeError*`
-- helper, so it is invisible to a grep for them — which is exactly how a refactor of the
-- diagnostic channel can miss it.  Before this fixture the message appeared nowhere in
-- test/ except the compiler's own rendered snapshot, i.e. nothing asserted the behaviour.
--
-- Shape: a `do` chain whose FINAL expression is a non-container (`Bool`) while `andThen`
-- requires the chain's monad shape (`Option b`).  `typeMismatchInDo` sees
-- `monoIsApp (TApp Option b) /= monoIsApp (TCon Bool)` and retargets the bare
-- `Type mismatch` to the tailored "do requires a monad" line, blaming the do-block.
--
-- Deliberately NOT `x <- <non-container>` (e.g. `x <- 5`): that shape is intercepted
-- first by `andThen`'s container-arg hint (`'andThen' expects a container …`) and never
-- reaches this path — verified.  Prelude-dependent (`Some`), so Driver B only.
main = do
  x <- Some 1
  True
